                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_589">Winchcombe,
                        Gloucestershire, Benedictine abbey of St Kenelm</orgName><p>The 1913 sale
                        catalogue (see below) notes that there is an illegible title-label on the
                        2nd cover of the medieval binding, and that the manuscript is 'probably from
                        Winchcombe monastery'. The wording shows that this tradition is based on a
                        reading of the label; compare the form of the ex libris inscription in <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_5713">Oxford,
                           Bodleian Library, MS Douce 368</ref>, Cope sale lot 9 (and <ref
                           target="https://mlgb.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/book_6736">Oxford, Jesus
                           College, MS 102</ref>).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners"><persName role="fmo">Cope</persName> sale, 4
                     March 1913 at Sotheby's, lot 171 to <persName role="fmo">Buddicom</persName>
                     for £2.2.0. This was the last known provenance according to the supplement to
                     Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1987). The book remains untraced; compare
                     the Schoenberg Database of Manuscripts <ref
                        target="https://sdbm.library.upenn.edu/entries/7291"
                     >SDBM_7291</ref>.</provenance>
               </history>
